While usually attributed to A.P. Carter the earliest recording was in 1927 by William Morris and it was likely in circulation in Appalachia prior to that.  The Carter family recorded it in 1929 and A.P. may have rewritten it.  I much prefer John Prine's upbeat version and it's that version the song is patterned after although the music is the same for either.

TIP:  The instrumental mandolin bridge repeats the chords from the verse.

TIP:  Play with a bluegrass snappiness.   


